WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
Hey, welcome to Planetarian Daily, episode 110.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.620
Today is July 4th, 2026.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:08.760
Let's see what the latest research is telling us.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.600
Intermittent fasting in an eight-hour window

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.900
raised median lifespan 12% in male mice.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.160
Timer-stricted feeding to an eight-hour window

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.980
produced a 12% gain in median lifespan in male mice.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.900
The benefit appears tied to voluntary calorie reduction

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.480
rather than timing alone.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:31.560
Female showed little or no effect under the same protocol.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.060
Follow-up work is testing whether the advantage holds

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.300
when calories are matched across groups.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:41.120
A few episodes back the show examined cellular aging

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:41.860
interventions.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.160
This study adds detail on how metabolic timing influences

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.280
lifespan outcomes in male mice.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:52.140
Researchers from Oxford's Environmental Change Institute

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.240
map disease patterns across the Brazilian Amazon

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.240
and found they align with specific combinations

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.120
of deforestation, agriculture, and rural economies

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.840
rather than occurring randomly.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.220
The study shows distinct regional signatures

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:09.280
for different insect vectors tied

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.080
to how people modify landscapes.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.180
These patterns emerge from interactions

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.720
between environmental change and local economic activities.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.520
Follow-up work will test whether targeted land management

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.020
changes can reduce transmission hotspots.

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.760
Genomic tools now allow direct influence

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.600
over species and ecosystems.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.540
Prompting researchers to examine how indigenous data rights

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.540
and ecological knowledge should shape their application.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.700
The discussion highlights historical human roles

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:43.220
in ecosystems and questions who controls genomic data

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.180
derived from indigenous lands.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.880
Current frameworks often overlook these governance issues.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.420
Next steps include developing protocols

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.500
that embed indigenous oversight into project design

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.440
from the outset.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.460
KISS engineers built a compact plug-and-play device

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.720
that generates single photons without cryogenic cooling

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.740
and operates once powered on.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.240
The 19-inch rack format removes the need

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:10.180
for specialized lab infrastructure.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:14.600
This moves quantum light sources toward practical deployment

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.240
outside research settings.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:19.580
Further engineering will focus on integrating the source

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.180
with existing quantum communication hardware.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.200
Along missing specimen allowed researchers

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.760
to reconstruct growth rates and life stages

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.000
of the extinct shark across its range.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:33.020
The analysis shows how the animal's size

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.800
and habitat use changed through ontogeny.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:39.020
Museum collections can still yield new data

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:40.620
when specimens resurface.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:43.900
Additional fossils will help refine estimates

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:46.260
of population structure before extinction.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:50.600
University of bond researchers tested two animal welfare

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.020
label posters in a virtual supermarket

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.540
and found the largest shift toward higher standard products

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.780
when both posters appeared together.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.300
Each poster alone produced smaller

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.880
but measurable changes in participant choices.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.760
The effect was tracked through actual items

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.260
placed in the virtual cart.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:10.860
Real world trials are planned to check

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.980
whether the pattern holds outside the lab.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:16.460
Teams from TU Dresdened, Max Planck,

00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.600
and Basel combined observed choices

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.960
with participants own written explanations of their reasoning.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.260
The method reveals motivations

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.640
that choice data alone cannot capture.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.520
Machine learning analysis of the text

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.200
identifies recurring patterns across individuals.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.780
Future studies will apply the approach

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:37.580
to larger and more diverse decision contexts.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:42.160
Scientists modified wheat to form supersized starch granules

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.300
inside the grain.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.360
The change opens possibilities for altered digestibility

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.720
and new industrial uses of the starch.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.520
The work demonstrates precise control

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.400
over a key storage compound

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.820
through targeted biological engineering.

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:01.060
Yield and processing trials will determine commercial viability.

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:05.460
A science advances study combined genetics, archaeology,

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.260
and anthropology to show that political power

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.880
among sithian elites passed through extended family lineages

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.960
spanning multiple burial grounds.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.840
The data indicate inherited authority

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:18.920
rather than purely local status.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.840
This revises earlier views of nomadic social structure.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.980
Additional genomes from under sampled regions

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:28.300
will test how widespread the pattern was.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.940
Now, shifting to a device level approach

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:33.720
that could one day restore function in human tissue.

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:37.100
A perfusion system maintains metabolic activity

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.900
in whole eyes retrieved from deceased donors.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.220
The approach supplies oxygen and nutrients

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.920
directly to retinal tissue.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.540
Earlier attempts failed because the eye lost function

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.200
before surgery could succeed.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:53.720
Human trials will assess whether restored eyes

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:56.360
can transmit visual signals after grafting.

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.140
The system creates a practical window

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:02.680
for surgical reconnection by maintaining retinal metabolism.

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:06.240
The next milestone is a controlled human pilot

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:09.080
measuring signal transmission from grafted tissue.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.660
Analysis of 430 samples with deep RNA seek

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:16.540
showed that graph-based methods detect expression

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:20.320
quantitative trait loci, involving structural variants

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.340
and multi-alelic indels missed by linear reference approaches.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:28.060
Power improved at 7.9% of genes

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:32.860
with 1.8% showing at least 50% gains in significance.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.700
The work also lifted median variants

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:38.000
explained in expression prediction models

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.920
from 10.1% to 12.5%.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.000
Larger cohorts will test translation

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.700
to complex disease traits.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.340
Review of 19 populations across eight genetic data sets

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:53.880
revealed that large clones and unclear population boundaries

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.260
systematically distort knee estimates

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.020
in ectomycorrhizal fungi.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:00.660
Both linkage disequilibrium

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:04.380
and subship frequency methods proved sensitive to these factors.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:07.680
The findings questioned current use of any

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.680
as a genetic indicator for conservation in species

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.340
with partial clonality.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.100
Refined sampling designs are needed

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.040
before the metric can reliably inform policy.

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:21.680
While one technology works to preserve tissue function,

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.880
the fossil record shows how entire marine communities

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:27.780
have responded to past warming by changing size.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:31.280
A multi-university study of the fossil record

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:34.420
documents consistent body size reduction in muscles,

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:37.100
crustaceans and fish during intervals

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:39.120
of strong global temperature rise.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:43.300
The lily put effect appears across hundreds of millions of years

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.740
and is most pronounced in the warmest phases.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:50.360
The pattern offers a long-term biological signal of climate stress.

00:06:50.900 --> 00:06:52.860
Modern monitoring programs will check

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:56.560
whether contemporary warming is producing similar size shifts.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:00.060
From present-day efforts to counteract tissue loss,

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.940
we look at a consistent biological pattern

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:06.240
that appeared whenever oceans warmed in the deep past.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:09.680
Shenzhen Institute's researchers created prints

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:13.160
and little prints systems that activate crisper only

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.640
in the presence of specific drug inducers

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.360
while remaining silent otherwise.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:21.240
The dual control design was tested in living tissues

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.140
to limit off target activity.

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:26.100
This approach addresses safety concerns

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.940
in therapeutic genome editing.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:30.760
Ongoing work will optimize delivery

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:33.920
and test longer-term stability in disease models.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.440
From engineered control of editing,

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:39.100
we examine how natural sampling behavior

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.560
is shared across mammals.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:44.520
Northwestern researchers found that mice, like humans,

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:47.680
use single deliberate sniffs to probe their surroundings

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.780
rather than only rapid sampling.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.960
Electrophysiological recordings confirmed

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:55.040
the controlled single-sniff behavior.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:57.560
The finding overturns the assumption

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:01.180
that rodents rely exclusively on high-frequency sniffing.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:04.940
The shared mechanism suggests conserved neural circuits

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:06.920
for active sensing across mammals.

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:09.860
Before we go, keep an eye on results

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.580
from the controlled human pilot

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:14.700
that will measure signal transmission from grafted retinas.

